  <name>Deskveet</name>
  <summary>Clean caches, keep control</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.vecvel">
    <name>vecvel</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>Deskveet shows where your disk space went and cleans what is safe to clean.</p>
    <p>Most full disks are full of things nobody chose to keep: build folders, package caches, browser caches,
      thumbnails and the downloads tools leave behind. Deskveet knows where these live, measures them, and tells you
      what each one is before anything is touched.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>See where your space went with a fast folder scan and a scrollable treemap</li>
      <li>Rules for the cache folder, thumbnails, browsers, apps and developer tools such as Gradle, npm, Cargo and pip</li>
      <li>Every rule says what you lose and how it comes back</li>
      <li>Preview everything first; items go to the Trash, with an undo log and Restore</li>
      <li>Find large old files and duplicate files by content</li>
      <li>Remove Flatpak apps, find what removed apps left behind, and see what starts when you log in</li>
      <li>System tray: clean safe caches, quit apps, keep awake, eject drives, lock, sleep, restart, shut down</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No accounts and no tracking. Its only connection is a daily check for updates, which you can turn off.</p>
  </description>
